  "worked_solution": "Let's denote the given statement as $P.$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\nIt is **not** true that $0.75$ does **not** belong to the set of rational numbers.\n\nIn other words, $0.75$ belongs to the set of rational numbers. Therefore, $¬P$ means the following:\n\n$0.75$ belongs to the set of rational numbers.\n\nNote that $P$ is **false,** while $¬P$ is **true.**",
